          "q": "What is semantic HTML and why does it matter?",
          "a": "Semantic HTML uses elements that describe their meaning, like header, nav, main, article, section, footer, button and table, instead of generic divs and spans. It gives screen readers and keyboard users landmarks to navigate, helps search engines understand page structure, provides built-in behavior such as focusable buttons, and makes markup easier to read and maintain.",
