          "id": "web-qwoyi",
          "q": "Explain the CSS box model and what box-sizing: border-box changes.",
          "a": "Every element is a box made of content, padding, border and margin. With the default content-box, width applies only to the content, so padding and border add to the rendered size. With border-box, width includes padding and border, which makes layouts predictable; most resets apply it globally with a universal selector. Margins are never included, and adjacent vertical margins can collapse.",
