          "q": "What is the difference between px, em, rem and viewport units, and which do you use for what?",
          "a": "px is absolute. em is relative to the current font size (the parent's when set on font-size itself), so it compounds in nested elements. rem is relative to the root font size, which respects user browser settings, so use it for type, spacing and media queries. vw and vh are percentages of the viewport, useful for fluid type with clamp(); prefer dvh on mobile, where 100vh ignores the address bar and can overflow the visible area.",
