          "q": "What is the difference between async and defer on a script tag?",
          "a": "A plain script blocks HTML parsing while it downloads and runs. async downloads in parallel and executes as soon as it arrives, in any order, which suits independent scripts like analytics. defer downloads in parallel but waits to run until parsing finishes, before DOMContentLoaded, preserving order, so it is the default choice for app code. Module scripts are deferred automatically.",
