          "q": "What happens between typing a URL into the browser and the page appearing on screen?",
          "a": "The browser checks its caches, resolves the hostname through DNS, opens a TCP connection (or QUIC for HTTP/3), performs the TLS handshake, and sends the HTTP request. The server responds with HTML; the browser parses it into the DOM, fetches CSS and scripts, builds the CSSOM and render tree, runs layout and paint, and composites layers to the screen, then fires DOMContentLoaded and load.",
