          "id": "design-z7xslh",
          "q": "Explain the CAP theorem and what it means in practice when you choose between consistency and availability.",
          "a": "During a network partition a distributed store must choose: refuse some requests to stay consistent, or answer with possibly stale data to stay available. Partitions are rare, so the daily trade-off is really latency versus consistency. Use strong consistency for money, inventory and auth; accept eventual consistency for feeds, counters and analytics, and handle replica lag with read-your-own-writes routing.",
