          "q": "How would you plan disaster recovery for a production database?",
          "a": "Define RPO, how much data you can lose, and RTO, how long you can be down. Enable automated daily backups plus point-in-time recovery from WAL, store copies in another region, and encrypt them. Test restores on a schedule, because untested backups are not backups. For a low RTO add a standby replica with automatic failover and write the runbook.",
